; rowsum_overflow: a row whose coefficients sum past i64::MAX must raise.
;
; linear = [i64::MAX, 1] on a 1x2 grid: the partial sum after the second
; column is 2^63, not representable, so ROWSUM raises ArithmeticOverflow
; rather than wrapping (SPEC.md overflow rule on coefficient reductions).

PUSH 2
BQMX r0

PUSH 1           ; rows
PUSH 2           ; cols
RESIZE r0

PUSH 0
PUSH 9223372036854775807
SETLINE r0
PUSH 1
PUSH 1
SETLINE r0

PUSH 0           ; row
ROWSUM r0
HALT
